## API keys (`ak`)

Approved low-risk secrets are GPG-encrypted in the WSL distro explicitly named
by `~/.config/ak/vault.conf` (currently `Debian-Recovered`, but managed
configuration may change it). Never use the default WSL distro implicitly,
search other distros, fall back to Windows Credential Manager, or automate
Bitwarden access.

{{ if eq .chezmoi.os "windows" -}}
On Windows (Git Bash/MSYS2), use the `windows-env` wrappers. They route only to
the configured named distro and fail closed when it is unavailable:

```bash
~/.pi/agent/skills/windows-env/ak-get brave
~/.pi/agent/skills/windows-env/ak-get --list
```
{{ else -}}
Inside the configured authoritative distro, use `ak` directly:

```bash
ak get brave
ak list
```
{{ end -}}

Across an environment boundary, use
`~/.pi/agent/skills/windows-env/ak-get`. The managed `~/.envrc`
is the reviewed export profile; import only its explicit service allowlist. Do
not use no-argument bulk loading or add `export: false` credentials. Never store
keys in plaintext dotfiles, and retrieve them only when explicitly required.

